      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive).\n\nCOMPOUND VERB: Formed from {持|も}つ (to hold) + かける (to apply/bring to). The combination conveys bringing something (usually a proposal) to someone.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n・{話|はなし}を{持|も}ちかける (bring up a topic/proposal)\n・{相談|そうだん}を{持|も}ちかける (approach with a consultation)\n・{取引|とりひき}を{持|も}ちかける (propose a deal)\n・{縁談|えんだん}を{持|も}ちかける (propose a marriage arrangement)\n\nUSAGE: Often used with passive form {持|も}ちかけられる when receiving a proposal. Can have slightly negative nuance when describing unsolicited or suspicious proposals.",
